---
/**
 * The "into BeltManager" half of every export guide (#30). One copy, so the four guides
 * cannot drift from the importer. Every rule here was read from the app's importer
 * (leavereview/beltmanager src/lib/services/student-import-csv.ts and student-import-plan.ts,
 * 7 Nov 2026): the headings it recognises, day-first dates, the phone rule, the guardian
 * rule for under-18s, active/trial status only, 1,000 rows a file, all-or-nothing commit,
 * and the 24-hour undo. If the importer changes, change this file.
 *
 * `variant` picks US or UK spelling and examples: Martialytics, Kicksite and Zen Planner
 * guides are US-weighted; the BMABA guide is UK.
 */
import { appLink } from '../../utils/appLink';

interface Props {
  variant: 'us' | 'uk';
  /** Tool name, used in the copy ("your Kicksite file"). */
  from: string;
}

const { variant, from } = Astro.props;
const us = variant === 'us';

const headings = [
  'First name',
  'Last name',
  'Date of birth',
  'Email',
  'Phone',
  'Guardian name',
  'Guardian email',
  'Guardian phone',
  'Group',
  'Current belt',
  'Status',
  'Medical notes',
  'Emergency contact name',
  'Emergency contact phone',
];
---

<section class="section bg-gray-50" id="import">
  <div class="container-custom max-w-3xl">
    <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-brand-navy mb-6">Import the file into BeltManager</h2>

    <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-brand-navy mb-3">First, tidy the file</h3>
    <ul class="space-y-3 text-gray-700 mb-8 list-disc pl-6">
      <li>
        <strong>Every student needs a date of birth.</strong> It's how BeltManager knows who is under 18 and needs a guardian.
        {us ? (
          <>BeltManager reads dates <strong>day first</strong> (DD/MM/YYYY) or as <strong>YYYY-MM-DD</strong>. Most US exports write month first, so <code>03/04/2015</code> (March 4) would be read as April 3. Change the birth date column to YYYY-MM-DD before you upload: in Excel or Google Sheets, select the column and set a custom date format of <code>yyyy-mm-dd</code>.</>
        ) : (
          <>Write dates as DD/MM/YYYY (for example <code>14/03/2016</code>) or YYYY-MM-DD. Two-digit years such as <code>14/03/16</code> are refused rather than guessed.</>
        )}
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Students under 18 need a guardian on the same row:</strong> a guardian name, plus a guardian email or phone. Siblings who share a guardian end up linked to the same guardian record.
      </li>
      <li>
        {us ? (
          <><strong>Phone numbers need the country code.</strong> Write them as <code>+1 555 010 0123</code>. A number without <code>+1</code> is refused. If your phone column isn't in that format, set it to "Don't import" and add numbers later.</>
        ) : (
          <><strong>Phone numbers must be mobiles.</strong> UK mobiles (07… or +44 7…) are accepted; landlines are refused. If your file has landlines, set that column to "Don't import" and add numbers later.</>
        )}
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Status can only be "active" or "trial".</strong> Remove students who have left, or set the status column to "Don't import" and everyone comes in as active.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Only bring what you need.</strong> Medical notes import if you map them, but leave out anything you don't need to run your classes safely.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Size:</strong> up to 1,000 students, 50 columns and 2 MB per file. Split a bigger file in two.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-brand-navy mb-3">Then import it</h3>
    <ol class="space-y-4 text-gray-700 mb-8 list-decimal pl-6">
      <li>Sign in to BeltManager as the school owner and open <strong>Students → Import</strong>.</li>
      <li>Choose your {from} CSV file. Want to see the expected layout first? Click <strong>Download template</strong>.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Match your columns.</strong> BeltManager {us ? 'recognizes' : 'recognises'} these headings automatically, and common variations such as "Parent email", "Belt", "Rank" or "Class":
        <ul class="mt-3 grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-x-6 gap-y-1 text-sm list-none pl-0">
          {headings.map((h) => (
            <li><code>{h}</code></li>
          ))}
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3">First name, Last name and Date of birth are required. Set any other column to <strong>"Don't import"</strong>.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Check every row.</strong> The preview shows what will happen to each student: created, updated, skipped or an error. A student already in BeltManager with the same name and date of birth is skipped, unless you tick "Update students who are already in BeltManager". If any row has an error, nothing is saved: fix those rows and check again.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Import.</strong> A <code>Group</code> name you don't have yet becomes a new group, and its students become its regulars. A <code>Current belt</code> you don't have yet is added to your belts: if you teach more than one style, write it as <code>Karate: Yellow</code> so BeltManager knows which ladder it belongs to.
      </li>
      <li>Changed your mind? You can <strong>undo an import within 24 hours</strong> from the import history on the same page.</li>
    </ol>

    <div class="card border-l-4 border-brand-red">
      <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-brand-navy mb-2">Card details never move by CSV</h3>
      <p class="text-gray-700">
        No spreadsheet carries a family's saved card, and BeltManager never takes card numbers from a file. {us ? (
          <>Card billing in BeltManager switches on in April 2027 for UK schools; for US schools it's coming in 2027. When it's available to your school, families add their card themselves.</>
        ) : (
          <>Card billing in BeltManager switches on in April 2027: when it does, families add their card themselves. Until then you can record payments by hand.</>
        )} Keep your {from} billing running until you're ready to switch it off.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p class="text-gray-700 mt-8">
      Stuck on a column? <a href="/contact/" class="text-brand-red hover:underline">Send us the file's column headings</a> (not the data) and we'll tell you how to map them.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-6">
      <a href={appLink(Astro.url.pathname, 'import-steps')} class="btn-primary">Get started free</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
